  "enhanced_information": "Male pattern baldness, also known as androgenetic alopecia, is characterized by hair follicle miniaturization due to increased levels of dihydrotestosterone (DHT) binding to androgen receptors. This leads to shortening of the anagen phase of the hair growth cycle and progressive hair loss. The most appropriate treatment for this condition is the administration of Finasteride, which inhibits the conversion of testosterone to DHT. Evidence supports the role of Finasteride in treating alopecia by targeting the underlying hormonal mechanism."
